rust-proxmox-access-log (0.1.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * filter: let the user filter match any user or API token that contains the
    text, ignoring case, like the search does, so that for example 'root'
    finds root@pam and its API tokens. An exact match still compares the whole
    ID, and an empty user filter counts as no filter.

  * report a compressed rotated copy as too large to read, if the first 32 MiB
    of its data hold no complete line, like a copy starting with skippable
    zstd frames. Such a copy could get skipped without reporting a gap, so a
    query took the log as complete.

  * statistics: count nothing as covered at an unterminated end of the log
    that is longer than one call reads, as it holds no complete line.

  * stop reading a compressed copy once the read budget of a call is used up,
    so that a read error after that fails the call instead of counting as the
    end of the budget.

  * read the same copy each time, if a rotated copy exists both compressed
    with gzip and with zstd, as after changing the compression.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:37:30 +0100

